  "description": "Contracts for strongly-typed wrappers that embed a primitive in the domain. IValueType<TSelf, TValue> is self-referential (CRTP) so its static abstract members resolve through the type parameter at every call site: three arrows in — the fallible lift Parse (string to Result<TSelf>), the checked embedding of a primitive the caller already holds, and the unchecked embedding for values the caller vouches for — and one arrow out, the projection back to the primitive. Validation lives in Checked, and Parse factors through it, so a lifted value is trusted everywhere downstream. ITryParse opts a type into the BCL bool-plus-out shape for ASP.NET model binding, without putting transport concerns in the domain contract.",
